= The Capitol Under Siege

On the day Congress meets to certify the election, an angry crowd stirred by claims of fraud storms the Capitol. Lawmakers flee. Police are overwhelmed. Hours later, order is restored and Congress completes its task.

Whatever the verdict of the courts, history will remember the day American democracy came closer to the edge than at any time in generations.

- @capitol_commission: Demand a full independent investigation
- @capitol_prosecute: Support prosecution of those responsible
- @capitol_move_on: Move on to the legislative agenda

@capitol_commission
on-arrival: capitol_done = year; institutions += 3; pro_democracy += 3; polarization += 2; maga_strength -= 3; farright_strength -= 2; militia_strength -= 60; gopmod_relation -= 3

A bipartisan commission is stymied; yet the investigation goes ahead and documents what happened.

@capitol_prosecute
on-arrival: capitol_done = year; institutions += 2; farright_strength -= 3; militia_strength -= 80; federal_law_loyalty += 0.03; polarization += 1; pro_democracy += 2

Hundreds of rioters face charges, with sentences that hit militia networks hard.

@capitol_move_on
on-arrival: capitol_done = year; working_dem += 2*(1-dissent); moderate_strength += 2; progressive_dissent += 4; institutions -= 1; pro_democracy -= 1

We want to turn the page, but the page does not turn.
